    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4004" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλεξ-ήτειρα</span></b> , ἡ, <i><span class="en">
			<u>AP</u>
			9.764
		</span></i> (Paul. Sil.), <i><span class="en">
			Nonn.
			<u>D.</u>
			25.529
		</span></i>: fem. of <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλεξ-ητήρ</span></b> ,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῆρος</span>, ὁ,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one who keeps off</i>,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. μάχης</span>
			<i>stemmer</i> of battle, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				20.396
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λοιμοῦ ἀ.</span>
			<i>a protector from</i> plague, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				2.519
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κακῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					14.1003.25
				</span></i>
			:—rare in Prose, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταῖς πατρίσιν ἀλεξητῆρες εἶναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Oec.</u>
					4.3
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as
			Adj., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θυμὸς ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Opp.
					<u>H.</u>
					4.42
				</span></i>
			.</div>
